+<body data-page="detection" data-crumb="02 · Detection &amp; Compliance">
+<div class="app">
+    <aside th:replace="~{layout :: sidebar}"></aside>
+    <div class="main">
+        <header th:replace="~{layout :: topbar}"></header>
+        <main class="content">
+
+            <div class="page-head">
+                <div>
+                    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tag" style="color:var(--s2);border-color:rgba(245,158,11,.35)">Stage 02</span> audit row → flag + jurisdiction tag</div>
+                    <h1 class="page-title"><span class="accent" style="--a:var(--s2)">Detection &amp; Compliance</span></h1>
+                    <p class="page-sub">The instant a decision is persisted, two rules decide whether it needs a second look. Flagged decisions are tagged with the disclosure standard their jurisdiction calls for — a pointer for a human reviewer, never a certification that the decision passes it.</p>
+                </div>
+                <div class="head-actions">
+                    <span class="endpoint"><span class="verb get">GET</span>/api/flagged</span>
+                    <button class="btn primary" data-open-inject="fraud">Test a fraud flag</button>
+                </div>
+            </div>
+
+            <div class="grid g-4">
+                <div class="card kpi"><div class="label"><i style="background:var(--s1)"></i>Decisions reviewed</div><div class="val" id="k-rev">—</div><div class="foot">every ingested decision, synchronously</div></div>
+                <div class="card kpi"><div class="label"><i style="background:var(--s2)"></i>Flagged</div><div class="val" id="k-flag">—</div><div class="foot" id="k-flag-f">&nbsp;</div><div id="k-flag-s"></div></div>
+                <div class="card kpi"><div class="label"><i style="background:var(--s2)"></i>Flag rate</div><div class="val" id="k-rate">—</div><div class="bar mt-14" style="--c:var(--s2)"><i id="k-rate-b" style="width:0"></i></div></div>
+                <div class="card kpi"><div class="label"><i style="background:#6b7280"></i>Cleared</div><div class="val" id="k-clr">—</div><div class="foot">no rule fired · no tag needed</div></div>
+            </div>
+
+            <div class="grid g-2 mt-14">
+                <div class="card rule" style="--c:#f87171">
+                    <div class="top">
+                        <span class="ri"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 21V4h11l-2 4 2 4H5"/></svg></span>
+                        <div><div class="label">Rule 1</div><h3>Always-flag fraud referrals</h3></div>
+                        <div class="fired"><b id="r1">0</b><span>fired</span></div>
+                    </div>
+                    <p>A fraud flag means the agent itself thinks something is wrong — so it always routes to compliance review, no statistics needed.</p>
+                    <div class="logic"><span class="kw">if</span> decisionType == <span class="s">"FRAUD_FLAG"</span> <span class="kw">and</span> outcome == <span class="s">"FLAGGED"</span><br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">→</span> flag, reason = <span class="s">"Fraud flag from {agent} routes to compliance review"</span></div>
+                </div>
+                <div class="card rule" style="--c:var(--s2)">
+                    <div class="top">
+                        <span class="ri"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 3v18h18"/><path d="M7 15l4-4 3 3 6-7"/></svg></span>
+                        <div><div class="label">Rule 2</div><h3>Denial-rate outlier</h3></div>
+                        <div class="fired"><b id="r2">0</b><span>fired</span></div>
+                    </div>
+                    <p>An agent that denies far more than it approves is a bias signal. Once it has enough history, each further denial above the threshold gets flagged.</p>
+                    <div class="logic"><span class="kw">if</span> outcome == <span class="s">"DENIED"</span> <span class="kw">and</span> agent.total ≥ <span class="v">5</span> <span class="kw">and</span> agent.denials / agent.total &gt; <span class="v">50%</span><br/>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="kw">→</span> flag, reason = <span class="s">"Denial rate for {agent} is X% over N decisions"</span></div>
+                </div>
+            </div>
+
+            <div class="grid g-wide mt-14">
+                <div class="card">
+                    <div class="card-h"><h3>Agent denial-rate monitor</h3><span class="sub">current cumulative rate per agent</span>
+                        <div class="right"><button class="btn sm ghost" id="reset-sim">Reset to production</button></div></div>
+                    <div class="whatif">
+                        <div style="--c:var(--s2)"><div class="lab"><span>What-if threshold</span><b id="thr-l">50%</b></div><input type="range" id="thr" min="10" max="90" step="5" value="50"/></div>
+                        <div style="--c:var(--s2)"><div class="lab"><span>Minimum sample</span><b id="min-l">5</b></div><input type="range" id="min" min="1" max="20" step="1" value="5"/></div>
+                        <div class="res"><b id="sim-res">—</b>agents in outlier zone</div>
+                    </div>
+                    <div id="meters"></div>
+                    <div style="padding:12px 16px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)">
+                        <div class="callout" style="--c:var(--s2)">
+                            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 11v5M12 8h.01"/></svg>
+                            <div><b>Simulation only.</b> Sliders recompute on today's data in your browser — the production rule stays at 50% over 5+ decisions (<code>aegis.detection.*</code> config).</div>
+                        </div>
+                    </div>
+                </div>
+                <div class="card">
+                    <div class="card-h"><h3>Jurisdiction tagging</h3><span class="sub">click to filter the queue</span></div>
+                    <div id="stds"></div>
+                    <div style="padding:12px 16px">
+                        <div class="callout" style="--c:var(--info)">
+                            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 5-3.4 8.5-8 9.5C7.4 20.5 4 17 4 12V6z"/></svg>
